    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0248" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1820 <hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >11/15</hi></note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State
                        (White)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-07-25">July 25, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Argentine Ambassador called and showed me a telegram from his Government
                    saying that the Brazilian Ambassador had suggested joint action by Argentina and
                    Brazil to prevent war between Bolivia and Paraguay. The Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs said that he had replied that Argentina was disposed to do so; that he
                    thought they could be most effective at present by insisting that Bolivia and
                    Paraguay continue the negotiations in Washington and, if for any reason they are
                    unable to come to an agreement on a pact of non-aggression, that the new
                    situation thus created be submitted to the Neutral Commission also.</p>
                <p>I showed Mr. Espil the telegram we had just received from the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs of Bolivia<anchor n="11" xml:id="d146-f1"/> and the draft reply which
                    the Neutrals were about to sign.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d146-f2"/> He said that
                    he supported this telegram and that he would tell his Government that the
                    Neutrals were doing everything they possibly could; that they were sending a
                    further telegram to Bolivia today, and that he would urge his Government to back
                    it up with good advice in La Paz and Asunción.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">hite</hi>] </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
